# Everything here runs on Linux. A clone must have LF endings whatever the
# platform it lands on: a \r in a sourced env file becomes part of a value, and
# in a script it is a bash syntax error. git normalises on commit and checks
# these out as LF even where core.autocrlf is true.
*           text=auto eol=lf
*.sh        text eol=lf
a5.env      text eol=lf
a5.env.*    text eol=lf
Dockerfile* text eol=lf
*.md        text eol=lf
